<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.10" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="18776-5" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Plan of care note"/>
    <title>Plan of Treatment</title>
    <text><list><item>Referral to clinical psychology for a trauma-informed diagnostic evaluation of nightmares, watchfulness, and short sleep, with trauma-focused psychotherapy (cognitive processing therapy or prolonged exposure) offered if he meets criteria for PTSD and wants it. Guideline: VA/DoD Clinical Practice Guideline for Management of Posttraumatic Stress Disorder and Acute Stress Disorder (2023); Trauma-Informed Care in Behavioral Health Services (Treatment Improvement Protocol 57) (2014) [S]</item><item>Trauma-informed care at every visit: explain each question, examination, and test before it happens and ask his agreement; offer a chaperone; let him choose what to share and stop at any time; no retelling of details is needed for his care. Guideline: VA/DoD Clinical Practice Guideline for Management of Posttraumatic Stress Disorder and Acute Stress Disorder (2023); Trauma-Informed Care in Behavioral Health Services (Treatment Improvement Protocol 57) (2014) [S]</item><item>Measurement-based follow-up: PCL-5 and PHQ-9 at each chronic-care visit and hand pain on a 0 to 10 scale at every visit. Guideline: VA/DoD Clinical Practice Guideline for Management of Posttraumatic Stress Disorder and Acute Stress Disorder (2023); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, rheumatoid arthritis and osteoarthritis monograph (2026); Depression and Suicide Risk in Adults: Screening (2023) [S]</item><item>Hand care: diclofenac 1% gel up to four times a day; six sessions with a hand therapist over eight weeks for range-of-motion and strengthening exercises and joint protection; a wide-barrel pen, a ten-minute break each hour of writing, and dictation for long drafts. Guideline: 2019 American College of Rheumatology/Arthritis Foundation Guideline for the Management of Osteoarthritis of the Hand, Hip, and Knee (2019); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, rheumatoid arthritis and osteoarthritis monograph (2026) [S]</item><item>A care plan built on the strengths he names: his work and writing, his family and community, and his faith, with visits scheduled around his travel for speaking. Guideline: VA/DoD Clinical Practice Guideline for Management of Posttraumatic Stress Disorder and Acute Stress Disorder (2023); Trauma-Informed Care in Behavioral Health Services (Treatment Improvement Protocol 57) (2014) [S]</item></list></text>

  </section>
